## §0 -- Foundational Requirements (inception only -- new project / new sprint)

> **Decide these BEFORE the six feature personas.** They are the expensive-to-reverse
> non-functionals -- the ones that, left unstated, surface as a 95%-done retrofit (the
> Node cross-platform port and the de-personalization scrub were both this exact bug class:
> Windows/personal defaults baked in silently). Answer all six EXPLICITLY -- never defaulted.
> Per `architect-first.md` §0.5 + `enforcement-first.md`, an inception artifact that declares
> `Foundational scope: inception` above MUST carry this section with all six fields filled.
> Gate: `scripts/verifiers/verify-foundational-requirements.mjs` (forge doctor).
> Feature-scoped artifacts set `Foundational scope: feature` and omit this section.

- **Target OS / platforms:** <Windows | macOS | Linux | web | mobile -- list EVERY target that must work>
- **Runtime / language:** <e.g. Node 20+ / Python 3.12 / Deno -- and is it available on ALL the targets above? note how that was verified>
- **Audience:** <me-only | others -- "others" forces portability + de-personalization from the FIRST commit, never as a retrofit>
- **Tenancy:** <single | multi -- per VIBE Rule 17; if multi, every UX-affecting value is per-user-configurable from day 1>
- **Distribution model:** <local | plugin | SaaS | installable -- determines packaging + secrets posture>
- **Data + privacy boundary:** <what data lives where; what must NEVER leave the device/tenant; which AI/external services see what>

