## §4 -- Two-way data flow (per `two-way-traceability.md`)

### Forward: where do numbers come FROM?

| Surface / number | Source rows (table + column) | Helper (file:line) | Source-kind value |
|---|---|---|---|
| <feature element> | <e.g. transactions.amount_cents> | <e.g. src/lib/finance/tax.ts:42> | <e.g. plaid> |

### Reverse: where do numbers GO TO?

For each new source row this feature creates, list every downstream surface that depends on it:

| Source row | Consumer surface(s) |
|---|---|
| <e.g. investment_accounts.balance_cents> | NetWorthCard, /networth page, Dashboard top-line, AI insights "Q4 retirement check" |

### Drill-down contract

- Every rendered number has a `<SourceTrace>` (or equivalent) that opens the contributing rows
- Every source row has a `<ConsumersIndex>` that shows where it's used
- AI outputs that cite numbers log to `ai_output_provenance` with `sources[]`

